---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { facts, operator, retentionChoices } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Support" description="Help with AlgoMinutes: recording, notes, minutes, retention and deleting your account, and how to contact us.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${operator.support}`}>{operator.support}</a> and we'll get back to you. In the app,
      <strong>Settings → Help &amp; Support</strong> sends us your message with your app version, so we can help faster.
      If you're using the beta, include your User ID from <strong>Settings</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need permission to record?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. Recording laws differ between places, and many require everyone's consent. Tell people you're recording
        before you start. AlgoMinutes shows a notice before every recording and asks you to confirm you have permission.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How long does a note take?</summary>
      <p>
        Usually a few minutes after you stop recording, depending on length. You can leave the app; AlgoMinutes
        notifies you when the note is ready, or if it couldn't be processed.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What are minutes?</summary>
      <p>
        Your plan includes a number of recording minutes. Settings shows how many you've used. A recording that fails
        to process doesn't use your minutes.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I delete a note?</summary>
      <p>Open the note and choose <strong>Delete</strong>. The note, its transcript and its recording are deleted.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can notes be deleted automatically?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. In <strong>Settings → Data retention</strong>, choose to keep notes until you delete them, or to delete
        them automatically after {retentionChoices()}.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>I used AlgoMinutes as a guest. What happens to my notes?</summary>
      <p>
        A guest's notes belong to a guest account on that device. To keep them, choose <strong>Create account</strong>
        in Settings and sign in with Apple or Google: your notes stay with you. If you sign out as a guest, you can't
        get back into that guest account or its notes.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I delete my account?</summary>
      <p>
        In the app, go to <strong>Settings → Delete my account</strong>. If you can't use the app, see
        <a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a>. Everything is deleted at once, and removed from backups
        within {facts.backupWindowDays} days.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Base>
